course: dictionary
lesson: 7289
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and the words around it show you which meaning is meant. The word pip is a good example. «Seeds cannot grow in your stomach, which is dark, very acidic and has no soil; swallowed pips simply pass through.» Here a pip is a seed, the small hard part inside fruit.
explain: Now read this: «Britain's speaking clock began in 1936, and the BBC's six "pips" have marked the hour since 1924.» These pips are short high sounds, like the time signal on the radio. The clues are the clock and the hour, not fruit.
explain: Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Then put your meaning into the sentence in place of the hard word and check it still makes sense. In a maths problem about dice, the pips are the dots. In sport, someone who is pipped at the post has been beaten by a tiny amount.
explain: Some meanings are informal. In British talk, to give someone the pip is to annoy them. The words around the word, and how they feel, tell you which meaning is right.
fact: A word can have several meanings, so always check the context.
fact: A pip can be a seed in fruit, a short high sound, or a small spot or symbol.
fact: To be pipped at the post means to be beaten by a very small amount.
fact: «Pips» can also mean the dots on a dice, which help you count the number rolled.
fact: The context tells you which meaning is right; swap your meaning in to check.
exercise: «A whole swallowed pip usually passes out unbroken.» What is a pip in this sentence? | A short high sound | *A small seed | A star on a uniform | A dot on a dice
exercise: In a maths lesson, the dice shows five pips. What are the pips? | *The dots on the dice | A sound on the radio | A star on an officer's uniform | Seeds in a lemon
exercise: «Ali was pipped at the post by a tiny margin.» What does pipped mean? | *Beaten by a very small amount | Lifted high in the air | Cut in half | Given a present
exercise: Which word in «An apple's seeds sit in five little rooms» means the same as pips? | Rooms | Apple | *Seeds | Five
test: «The last pip marks the exact start of the hour.» What is a pip here? | *A short high sound | A seed inside fruit | A dot on a dice | A tiny bee
test: To give someone the pip means: | To tell them a joke | To make them fall asleep | To give them a present | *To annoy them
exam: «A tree grown from an apple pip gives apples that differ from the parent.» Why? | A pip is always a dot | Apples always taste the same | Pips never grow into trees | *Each pip has two parents, so it can differ from either of them
